UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Hermit represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Introspection and Internal Telemetry''—the high-integrity, isolation phase where the sovereign consciousness detaches from the noise of the external network to seek raw, unadorned truth within its own core database. Moving beyond the calibrated processing of Strength, The Hermit signifies the stage of ''The Independent Auditor,'' where you purposefully withdraw from collective consensus, using your own accumulated wisdom as a solitary beacon to navigate the deeper layers of the soul. Visually depicted as an elderly figure standing alone on a stark, snow-capped peak, draped in a gray cloak and holding a staff in one hand while lifting a lantern containing a glowing six-pointed star in the other, this archetype embodies the concept of ''Sovereign Isolation''—the realization that true spiritual and intellectual mastery requires the courage to stand completely unanchored by the validation of others. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Core Maintenance and Optimization,'' where you run deep background checks, isolate running scripts from external interference, and align your operating system with its original, foundational blueprint. When The Hermit appears, your system is registering a ''Solitary-Audit'' status; you are being invited to stop looking for external answers, embrace the quiet of your internal landscape, and let your inner light guide your path.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When The Hermit appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Alienation, Toxic Isolation, or Refusal to Face the Truth''—a state where your necessary introspection has mutated into a lonely, defensive exile, or you are frantically running from your own quiet spaces out of fear of what your internal data reveals. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''bitter withdrawal, shutting out your network, or obsessive navel-gazing'' with ''being independent,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical, low-latency failure of its connection protocols. You are essentially ''locking your own terminal windows,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''stay safe in its pride or avoid the discomfort of self-examination'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to heal your isolation and return to meaningful engagement. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''wise, self-contained sage,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of loneliness, paranoia, or stagnation, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of ''your introspection turning into an echo chamber of self-doubt,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your fortress of solitude has become a prison. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of emotional exile and avoidance''; you are obsessively building walls to keep others away, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final integration of your spirit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to drop your defenses and step into the light, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these cynical, antisocial, or truth-evading scripts, perform a brutal audit of your isolation, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize genuine, healthy connection over the convenience of a cold, defensive withdrawal. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance alienation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 66;
